# Prettier owns code formatting. It does not own generated output or
# hand-curated data files, for two different reasons.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. GENERATED ARTIFACTS - reformatting these breaks the build.
#
# These are emitted by canonicalJson (sorted keys, 2-space, trailing newline)
# and CI asserts they regenerate byte-identically. If Prettier rewrote them,
# `git diff --exit-code content/schema` would fail on every run and rule
# BLD-DETERMINISM-001 would report drift that isn't real.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
content/schema/
content/projects/
fixtures/
pnpm-lock.yaml
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. TABULAR DATA FILES - formatting carries meaning here.
#
# Budgets and vocabularies are written one entry per line so they read as
# tables. PRD 12.2 requires a budget change to be visible in review, and a
# one-line diff shows that better than a six-line one. Prettier would explode
# each entry across multiple lines and make the review harder, not easier.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config/*.json
content/taxonomy/*.json
content/editorial/*.json
